==English==

===Etymology===
[[onomatopoeic|Onomatopoeic]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɪf/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-biff.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪf|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[sudden]], [[sharp]] [[blow]] or [[punch]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1945|author=C. S. Lewis|title=The Great Divorce|passage="Hit him a '''biff'''," said the Big Man.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|sports}} A [[wipeout]].
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{euph form|en|bitch}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|en|biffo}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To [[punch]] or [[hit]].
# {{lb|en|Atlantic Canada|NZ|slang|transitive}} To [[discard]]; to [[throw out]]; to [[throw away]].
# {{lb|en|informal|sports}} To [[wipe out]]; to faceplant; to fall.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To move quickly.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{non-gloss definition|The sound of a person being punched or hit.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=5 Jun 1989|journal=The Canberra Times|location=Australia Capital Territory|page=10|column=2|text=Whap, '''Biff''', Ooooof, Sock, Pow, Zok! ''Batman'' is back. Gotham City is again leaving its law and order in the hands of a man who wears plastic underpants over his tights.}}

